    "# 1. Dataset Overview\n",
    "\n",
    " ### **What is this dataset?**\n",
    "The **StockTwits Sentiment Dataset** represents a high-resolution longitudinal archive of micro-blogging discourse specifically centered on the **SPDR S&P 500 ETF Trust (SPY)**. Covering the biennial window from April 2020 to April 2022, this dataset captures a high-frequency digital footprint of market participant expectations during a period defined by extreme pandemic-induced volatility and the unprecedented surge in retail trading activity.\n",
    "\n",
    "As discussed in the literature regarding the democratization of financial information, these data streams constitute a vital form of **behavioral alternative data**. While conventional fundamental and technical indicators are often criticized for their periodic nature and inherent reporting lags, social sentiment provides a real-time proxy for **\"Investor Attention\"** and **\"Crowd Sentiment\"** (Da et al., 2011). In informationally dense environments, such nontraditional signals act as a mechanism for price discovery, helping to resolve persistent information asymmetries and providing a quantitative lens into the psychological drivers of market liquidity (Renault, 2017; Goldstein et al., 2021).\n",
    "\n",
    "### **Key Features**\n",
    "\n",
    "| Category | Count | Description |\n",
    "| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n",
    "| **Total Messages** | ~3.27M | High-frequency investor discourse records |\n",
    "| **Asset Focus** | 10+ Tickers | Strong SPY dominance with megacap (AAPL, TSLA) co-mentions |\n",
    "| **Sentiment** | 3 Classes | Qualitative labels: Bullish, Bearish, and Neutral |\n",
    "| **Temporal Data** | Milliseconds | High-precision Unix timestamps for market synchronization |\n",
    "| **NLP Features** | Unstructured | Raw text strings suitable for transformer-based (FinBERT) analysis |\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "### **Environment Setup and Library Configuration**\n",
    "We begin by importing the necessary libraries for data processing, natural language handling, and neural network implementation."
