    "\n",
    "*   **Quantifying Informational Entropy:** The empirical evidence identifies the \"Neutral\" category as the dominant class, comprising approximately **56%** of the dataset. This finding aligns with the theoretical framework of **Antweiler and Frank (2004)**, which posits that behavioral datasets are characterized by a high signal-to-noise ratio. The prevalence of ambiguous signals necessitates the use of robust filtering and dimensionality reduction to extract meaningful market signals.\n",
    "*   **Systemic Optimism Bias:** There is a pronounced **Bullish skew** in the directional labels during the 2020–2022 observation window. This suggests that market participants on the StockTwits platform maintained a regime of systemic optimism regarding the S&P 500, even during periods of significant macroeconomic shifts. Such skews are common in retail investor communities and can serve as a proxy for herding behavior or \"crowd sentiment\" (Da et al., 2011).\n",
