    "# 4. Market Interconnectedness (Ticker Analysis)\n",
    "\n",
    "### **Computational Mapping of Asset Interconnectedness and Sentiment Propagation**\n",
    "\n",
    "Modern financial discourse within digital ecosystems is rarely isolated to a single asset; rather, it reflects a complex network of \"asset-centric\" interactions where mentions of various securities frequently overlap. As established in the literature regarding **Network Effects in Finance**, understanding the degree of interconnectedness between different assets is vital for capturing the systemic risks and macroeconomic themes that drive broad market indices (**Billio et al., 2012**). By extracting \"cashtags\"—the high-frequency metadata identifiers for specific equities—we can quantify the \"centrality\" of individual megacap stocks and evaluate their influence on the aggregate sentiment of the **SPY ETF**.\n",
    "\n",
    "In this section, we apply a **Natural Language Processing (NLP)** approach using **Regular Expressions (Regex)** to perform automated feature extraction from unstructured textual data. This methodology converts high-entropy market chatter into a structured mapping of co-mentions. This allows for the identification of **\"Sentiment Spillover\"** or cross-asset contagion effects, where idiosyncratic volatility in specific sectors (e.g., the technology sector represented by `$AAPL` or `$QQQ`) propagates through the broader market, influencing the risk premiums of diversified indices (**Diebold and Yilmaz, 2012**)."
